from pathlib import Path
import json,html
from PIL import Image,ImageDraw
from math import ceil,floor
root=Path('output/pin-basis');e=json.loads((root/'evaluation.json').read_text());rows=e['rows'];e512=json.loads((root/'evaluation512.json').read_text())
changes={str(n):{key:{m:100*(1-evidence['rows'][2]['regions'][key][m]/evidence['rows'][1]['regions'][key][m]) for m in ['mse','edgeMse']} for key in ['face','eyes','nose','mouth']} for n,evidence in [(384,e),(512,e512)]}
(root/'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(positiveMeansErrorReduction=True,versusFreshEqualBudgetControl=changes,qualityAcceptance='inconclusive; not promoted',physicalAcceptance=False),indent=2))
sheet=Image.new('RGB',(1200,660),'#faf8ef');d=ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)
for j,row in enumerate(rows):
 d.text((j*400+8,8),row['name']+' / native160',fill='#18201d');sheet.paste(Image.open(root/(row['name']+'-native.png')),(j*400+8,30));d.text((j*400+8,210),'All actual strands / common384',fill='#18201d');sheet.paste(Image.open(root/(row['name']+'-common.png')),(j*400+8,235))
sheet.save(root/'comparison.png')
settings=json.loads(Path('output/circle-head-240/circle-settings.json').read_text());feature=Image.new('RGB',(900,540),'#faf8ef');d=ImageDraw.Draw(feature)
for y,key in enumerate(['eyes','nose','mouth']):
 box=settings['portrait']['regions'][key];l=ceil(box['left']*159);t=ceil(box['top']*159);r=floor((box['left']+box['width'])*159)+1;b=floor((box['top']+box['height'])*159)+1
 for x,name in enumerate(['target','reference','control-240','basis-320']):
  p=Path('output/circle-head-240/circle-target.png') if name=='target' else root/(name+'-native.png');feature.paste(Image.open(p).crop((l,t,r,b)).resize((210,120),Image.Resampling.BILINEAR),(x*225+4,y*180+30));d.text((x*225+4,y*180+8),name+' / '+key,fill='#18201d')
feature.save(root/'features.png')
body='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Ip Rasm 240/320 pin basis</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;margin:24px;background:#faf8ef;color:#18201d;max-width:1250px}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce2d4;text-align:left}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#235544}.scroll{overflow:auto}</style><h1>Separate 240/320-pin chord basis experiment</h1><p>Same owner-local source, processed target, crop, unrotated 400x400mm board, 0.1mm thread and provisional 32-chord/160-incident winding guards. Both v11 fits start from an EMPTY optical graph, with no preserved seed, eight sweeps, identical maximum connection allowance and edge weight2. The older 240-pin reference is shown separately; it is not a comparable fresh-run control. The requested angular exclusion is7.5 degrees: discrete 240-pin gap5 gives7.5 degrees; 320-pin gap7 rounds up to7.875 degrees. Pin count and corresponding coordinate/angular discretization are disclosed. No legacy guide can be reused on the new board. The corrected fresh-basis initial tone loss matches its target-luminance penalty, including light-thread recovery. Unaccepted earlier artifacts are preserved separately; recalculation keeps both executable hashes unchanged.</p><p><b>Quality remains inconclusive; defaults are unchanged.</b> At common384 the new320 fit worsens eye and nose tone/contour error. Lip results are mixed, and neither fresh fit beats the preserved portrait reference. Eight sweeps are an equal compute allowance, not proof of full convergence or a general conclusion about every320-pin solver. Full observed generation takes longer and thread increases. Timings were recorded on a shared host with other local verification work; they are not isolated performance benchmarks. No likeness acceptance, physical acceptance or quality-preserving action savings is claimed.</p><h2>Ordinary native portraits and physical common384 replay</h2><p>Complete immutable sequences include every routing connection; no photo overlay, invented anatomy or result-specific sharpening.</p><img src="comparison.png" alt="Actual preserved portrait and fresh 240/320 strand reconstructions"><h2>Same source-derived feature windows</h2><img src="features.png" alt="Unchanged target and complete strand facial details"><h2>Exact material and compute evidence</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Connections</th><th>Estimated thread</th><th>Full generation</th></tr>'''
for row in rows:
 evidence={} if row['name']=='reference' else json.loads((root/(row['name']+'.json')).read_text())['evidence'];timing='Preserved older seeded reference; not rerun' if not evidence else f"{evidence['fullStageMs']/1000:.2f}s / fresh empty start"
 body+=f"<tr><td>{row['name']}</td><td>{row['connections']}</td><td>{row['meters']:.3f}m; +{max(0,row['meters']-600):.3f}m beyond600m</td><td>{timing}</td></tr>"
body+='</table></div><h2>Common384 and independently prepared common512 differences</h2><p>Positive: error reduction. Negative: worsening. Identical canonical source, source-remapped windows and physical thread geometry for each grid. These metrics do not establish human likeness.</p><pre>'+html.escape(json.dumps(changes,indent=2))+'</pre><p><a href="evaluation.json">Exact preview and production offline evidence</a> · <a href="evaluation512.json">Independent512 evaluation</a> · <a href="common-target.png">Canonical384 target</a> · <a href="common-target512.png">Canonical512 target</a> · <a href="control-240-guide.pdf">Complete240 guide</a> · <a href="basis-320-guide.pdf">Complete320 guide</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:4183/">Website</a></p></html>'
(root/'report.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf8');print(json.dumps(changes))
